Ladybird looks up the record of each animation sample by a key of what
it holds, and shares one record among the samples that hold the same
style. The other engines never look up a sample by what it holds, so
nothing like the cost this fixes arises in them. Blink applies animated
values in StyleResolver::ApplyAnimatedStyle(), after its
MatchedPropertiesCache lookup by matched declarations. WebKit’s
TreeResolver::createAnimatedElementUpdate() applies an element’s
animations to a style it has already resolved. And Gecko’s
StyleSharingCache::insert_if_possible() leaves out any element with
running animations, while its test_candidate() refuses to share a style
with or from an element that has them.
